{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794331640,"nonce":"Bti9OBFVyN6WjnzDoNq7P5mi36A=","message":"Coverage and conformance, direct backend, macOS (commit follows 9287d8ae). Reference type (every heap value is an i32): unit program 306 -\u003e 2162 functions direct (3.5% -\u003e 24.9%) from admitting it; null, null check (new runtime fn hlp_null_access), object field get/set at layout offsets, global slots and type constants through data symbols the pipeline exports: 3469 of 8688 (39.9%). Tool: crates/ash/examples/wasm_direct_coverage.rs (offline, no LLVM) groups the reasons a function was declined. Remaining top reasons in unit.hl: New 1401, virtual-object fields 1141, ToDyn 611, native calls 558, SafeCast 261, EnumField 138, trap regions 114, CallMethod 111, StaticClosure 111, MemGet 110. Bugs found only by running the whole suite with wider coverage: (1) a Haxe method named close collided with libc's in the runtime object - direct-touched functions are now renamed ash_direct_\u003cfindex\u003e; (2) taking a function's address in PIC code from another object used a GOT entry the linker only has for data - such functions are now hidden; (3) equality on references must go through hlp_dyn_compare for HDYN/HNULL/HOBJ/HVIRTUAL and compare addresses otherwise (unit.issues.Issue6710 caught it: boxed 2000000 == 2000000 was false). Results: unit suite 1069/1069 cases and 10971/10971 assertions on the wasm arm and on the wasm-fibers arm with 3469 functions direct; the harness modules were confirmed byte-identical to fresh direct builds. The direct wasm module is 18,448,666 bytes against 20,385,059 for LLVM-only (-9.5%). Regression tests: wasm_direct_mixed now covers TestWasmNumeric and TestWasmDynamic (equality, null access, fields of every kind, globals, type constants), with and without fibers.","files":null}]}